Accounting: did we get expenses in the net formula?
Partially — and the naming is inconsistent, which is risky.

Your formula:

Net sales = Gross sales − Total refunds − Total expenses

That matches what the dashboard calls “Net Today” (today_net_after_expenses) and what the sales trend calls net_revenue:

export function netSalesForDay(gross: number, refunds: number, expenses: number): number {
  return Math.max(0, gross - refunds - expenses);
Backend ReportMetricsService does the same at day level:

Field	Formula	Used where
gross_sales
Sum of sale.total_amount
Dashboard, Sales Trend, Daily Sales
net_sales
Gross − refunds
My Shift headline, per-sale net
net_revenue
Gross − refunds − expenses
Dashboard “Net Today”, Sales Trend
Where it’s correct today
Dashboard API — full formula ✓
Sales Trend report — Gross, Refunds, Expenses, Net Revenue per day + period totals ✓
Where it’s incomplete or misleading
Report	Issue
Daily Sales
Per-sale Net = gross − refunds only (correct per receipt). Period total does not subtract expenses — so it won’t match dashboard “Net Today” for the same dates.
Expenses
Lists expenses only — no bridge: “After these expenses, net sales for the period is X.”
Payment Breakdown
Net = gross − refunds per method (correct for collections). Expenses are intentionally excluded (they affect cash handover, not card/mobile totals — same as My Shift).
Inventory
No P&L connection (fine for stock, but doesn’t answer profitability).
Recommendation for approval: adopt one label everywhere:

Net sales = gross − refunds (operating sales)
Net after expenses = gross − refunds − expenses (what dashboard “Net Today” shows)
Or use your single formula and rename dashboard fields to match. Right now “net” means different things on different screens.

