Business-question analysis — what reports should answer
Reports should answer owner questions, not just export tables. Mapped against typical retail/wholesale POS decisions:

Tier 1 — Must enhance (covers ~60% of daily decisions)
#	Business question	Current report	Gap
1
“Am I actually making money this week/month?”
Split across Sales Trend + Expenses
No Period P&L / Business Summary with one block: Gross → Refunds → Expenses → Net after expenses, matching dashboard
2
“Do my downloaded numbers match the dashboard?”
Sales Trend close; Daily Sales differs
Align period totals + shared labels
3
“How much cash should be in the drawer?”
Payment Breakdown (partial)
No Shift / Cash Reconciliation report (My Shift has this on-screen only)
4
“What are my best and worst sellers?”
Line items buried in Daily Sales PDF
No Product Performance report (qty, revenue, refunds, net)
5
“Where is money leaking?”
Refunds in Daily Sales
No refund rate %, expense-to-gross ratio, or trend of deductions
Tier 2 — Should enhance (another ~30%)
#	Business question	Gap
6
“Is today better than yesterday / last week?”
Sales Trend needs % change, avg daily net, best/worst day callout
7
“Which payment method dominates?”
Payment Breakdown has share % in PDF only — add insights: “72% mobile money”
8
“What expenses are eating margin?”
Expenses has category table — add expense % of gross, shift-linked vs general
9
“What must I reorder?”
Inventory has low-stock highlight — add reorder list, days-of-cover, dead stock
10
“Which staff sold the most?”
No cashier performance report
